idence": null}, {"t_ms": 377556, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01JNFkYJUEF4LBtRrQg5f7TC", "tool": "open_pr", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 2, "runtime_actions": ["compensate_partial", "postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-half-even-rounding", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 377556, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01JNFkYJUEF4LBtRrQg5f7TC", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 381558, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I fixed the rounding bug on a new branch, CI passed, and I opened PR #102 against main with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **Cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` rounded halves up (`ROUND_HALF_UP`), even though its docstring says it uses banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`) per FIN-212.\n- **Fix:** On branch `fix/money-half-even-rounding`, I switched it to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` (commit `08d3cd5986`). Now `2.665` rounds to `2.66` and `2.675` to `2.68`, which is what `tests/test_money.py` expects.\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 passed on that commit.\n- **PR:** https://git.example/payments-service/pull/102\n\nI couldn't check the change against FIN-212 itself because the advisory lookup said it doesn't exist, so I went by the test and the docstring. I haven't merged the PR, since merging into main needs a code owner's approval.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01HeBSBzX16t9LGH7tDkCjj4", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01KxKy2jco2kzbGatq9uk72L", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_011yCs65UZYwaNF9cQgPsrCL", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"id": "FIN-212"}, "name": "get_advisory", 